.TH PRIVAI 1 "September 2026" "privai 1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
privai \- privacy-first terminal chat with a local Ollama model for development
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B privai
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B privai
is a terminal user interface for chatting with a local Ollama model.
Each question is sent with a snapshot of the current directory
(the first 20 lines of
.BR "ls -la" )
and, inside a git repository, the output of
.B git status --short
and
.BR "git log --oneline -5" .
Earlier turns of the conversation are sent as history.
Replies stream into a scrollable chat view as they are generated.
Nothing is sent anywhere except the configured Ollama server.
.SH OPTIONS
None.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B Enter
Send the message.
.TP
.BR Up ", " Down ", " PgUp ", " PgDn
Scroll the chat. Works while typing.
.TP
.B Esc
Leave the input box. The chat can then also be scrolled with
.BR j / k ,
.BR space / b
and
.BR u / d .
.TP
.B Tab
Return to the input box.
.TP
.B q
Quit, when the input box is not focused.
.TP
.B Ctrl+C
Quit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B OLLAMA_BASE_URL
Ollama server address. Default: http://localhost:11434
.TP
.B OLLAMA_MODEL
Model to chat with. Default: llama3.2
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/local/bin/privai
The program.
.TP
.I /usr/local/share/man/man1/privai.1
This manual page.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ollama (1),
.BR git (1)
